cs1lib.py is not my work.

It is the teaching graphics library written for Dartmouth's COSC 1
course, included here only because the three projects import it and
cannot run without it. It is not covered by the MIT licence in this
directory, which applies to my own code.

The projects import it as `from cs1lib import *`, so run them from
this directory:

    python3 -m nbody_simulation.solar
    python3 city_sorting/sort_cities.py
    python3 campus_pathfinding/map_plot.py

or copy cs1lib.py into the project folder you want to run.

city_sorting note: city.py parses world_cities.txt, the raw source
data, which I no longer have. Its output, cities_out.txt, is included,
so quicksort.py, sort_cities.py and visualize_cities.py all run. Only
the initial parsing step cannot be re-executed.
